---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import LanguageSwitch from '../../components/LanguageSwitch.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Thomas Kolonko – Business Coaching"
  description="Privacy information about this website, its hosting, contact by email and online appointment booking."
  language="en"
  alternatePath="/datenschutz/"
>
  <header class="sticky top-0 z-50 bg-stone-50/90 backdrop-blur-md border-b border-stone-200/80">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 h-20 flex items-center justify-between">
      <a href="/en/" class="font-serif text-xl font-medium tracking-tight text-slate-900">
        Thomas Kolonko <span class="text-stone-400 font-sans text-sm font-normal ml-1 hidden sm:inline">| Business Coaching</span>
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-6">
        <LanguageSwitch language="en" deHref="/datenschutz/" enHref="/en/privacy/" />
        <a href="/en/" class="text-sm font-medium text-emerald-800 hover:text-emerald-950 transition-colors">
          <span class="sm:hidden">← Home</span><span class="hidden sm:inline">← Back to home</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="py-16 md:py-24 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto bg-white p-8 sm:p-12 rounded-2xl border border-stone-200/80 shadow-xs space-y-8 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
      <div>
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-emerald-800 mb-2">Swiss Federal Act on Data Protection (FADP)</p>
        <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-slate-900 tracking-tight">Privacy policy</h1>
      </div>

      <section class="space-y-3 text-sm sm:text-base">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-xl text-slate-900 font-medium">1. General information and data controller</h2>
        <p>
          Under Article 13 of the Swiss Federal Constitution and the federal data protection provisions (Federal
          Act on Data Protection, FADP), everyone is entitled to privacy and protection against the misuse of
          their personal data. We take the protection of your personal data seriously and handle it
          confidentially and in accordance with applicable data protection laws and this privacy policy.
        </p>
        <p>
          The controller responsible for processing personal data on this website is:<br />
          <strong>Thomas Kolonko</strong><br />
          [Enter street and house number]<br />
          8000 Zurich, Switzerland<br />
          Email: <a href="mailto:info@thomaskolonko.ch" class="text-emerald-800 hover:underline">info@thomaskolonko.ch</a>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3 text-sm sm:text-base">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-xl text-slate-900 font-medium">2. Hosting and server log files (GitHub Pages)</h2>
        <p>
          This website is hosted as a static website on <strong>GitHub Pages</strong>, a service provided by
          GitHub Inc., 88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. St, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA (or GitHub B.V., Vijzelstraat
          68-72, 1017 HL Amsterdam, Netherlands).
        </p>
        <p>
          When you visit this website, GitHub automatically collects server log files to ensure technical
          operation and IT security. These may include your IP address, the date and time of access, browser
          type and operating system. Transfers of data to the USA rely on Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs)
          and the Swiss-U.S. Data Privacy Framework. For more information, see
          <a href="https://docs.github.com/de/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-emerald-800 hover:underline">GitHub’s privacy statement</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3 text-sm sm:text-base">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-xl text-slate-900 font-medium">3. No tracking cookies or externally hosted fonts</h2>
        <p>
          This website deliberately does not use analytics or advertising cookies (such as Google Analytics).
          All fonts are hosted locally, so loading the website does not connect to third-party font servers
          such as Google Fonts.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3 text-sm sm:text-base">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-xl text-slate-900 font-medium">4. Contact by email (Hostpoint)</h2>
        <p>
          If you contact us by email, we store the information you provide, including your contact details, to
          handle your enquiry and any follow-up questions. Our email infrastructure and domain management are
          provided by the Swiss company <strong>Hostpoint AG</strong> (Neue Jonastrasse 60, 8640
          Rapperswil-Jona, Switzerland), so your email communications are processed on servers in Switzerland.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3 text-sm sm:text-base">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-xl text-slate-900 font-medium">5. Confidentiality in the coaching process</h2>
        <p>
          All information, topics and documents discussed during an initial conversation or coaching or
          mentoring engagement are treated as strictly confidential and will never be shared with third parties
          – including clients or employers – without your express consent.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3 text-sm sm:text-base">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-xl text-slate-900 font-medium">6. Your rights under Swiss data protection law</h2>
        <p>
          Under applicable data protection law, you have the right at any time to obtain, free of charge,
          information about your stored personal data, its source and recipients, and the purpose of processing.
          You may also have the right to request correction, disclosure or deletion of this data. If you have
          questions about data protection, please contact us using the email address provided in the legal notice.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3 text-sm sm:text-base">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-xl text-slate-900 font-medium">7. Online appointment booking (Cal.com)</h2>
        <p>
          We use the online calendar service <strong>Cal.com</strong> (Cal.com, Inc., 548 Market St, PMB 80370,
          San Francisco, CA 94104, USA) to arrange introductory calls and coaching sessions. If you book
          through the embedded calendar widget, the information you enter – in particular your name, email
          address and any notes about your situation – is processed solely to organise the appointment and add
          it to our calendar. Transfers of data rely on Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) and the Swiss-U.S.
          Data Privacy Framework. For more information, see
          <a href="https://cal.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-emerald-800 hover:underline">Cal.com’s privacy policy</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 pt-4 border-t border-stone-200">
        English translation for convenience. In case of any discrepancy, the German version prevails.<br />
        Version: October 2026 · Zurich
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>

  <footer class="bg-stone-100 border-t border-stone-200/80 py-10 px-6 text-sm text-slate-500">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
      <div>© {new Date().getFullYear()} Thomas Kolonko · Zurich</div>
      <div class="flex gap-6">
        <a href="/en/legal-notice/" class="hover:text-slate-900 transition-colors">Legal notice</a>
        <a href="/en/privacy/" class="text-slate-900 font-medium">Privacy</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>
</Layout>
